course: dictionary
lesson: 14080
title: Mechanism: parts that work together
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A mechanism is a set of moving parts that work together to do a job. A clock has a mechanism inside that turns the hands. «The clock has a small mechanism inside that moves the hands.» You cannot see the hands moving all at once, but the parts are pushing and turning each other.
explain: Mechanism can also mean a way that something happens. «Our bodies have a mechanism for keeping warm: we shiver when we are cold.» Here there are no wheels or gears, just a system that works in the body. When you meet mechanism, ask: is it a machine with parts, or a system that makes something happen?
explain: Some mechanisms protect us. «The lift has a safety mechanism that stops it falling.» A safety mechanism is a machine part whose job is to keep people safe. Animals and people can have defence mechanisms too, which are ways of protecting themselves.
fact: A mechanism is a set of moving parts in a machine that work together.
fact: Examples of machine mechanisms include levers, gears, pulleys and cams.
fact: «Mechanism» can also mean a way or system by which something happens or is done.
fact: «The body's mechanism for keeping warm» includes shivering and sweating.
fact: A «safety mechanism» stops a machine from hurting people.
exercise: «The clock has a mechanism inside that moves the hands.» What is a mechanism here? | A loud alarm bell | A kind of cloth for the face | *A set of moving parts that work together | A small battery only
exercise: «Our bodies have a mechanism for keeping warm.» What does mechanism mean in this sentence? | A hat for cold weather | A warm blanket | A part of a bicycle wheel only | *A way or system by which something happens
exercise: «The lift has a safety mechanism that stops it falling.» What does the safety mechanism stop the lift doing? | *Falling | Climbing the wall | Opening its doors | Singing
test: Which of these is a mechanism you could build from moving parts? | A rainy day | A cup of tea | *A pulley | A quiet song
test: What is a defence mechanism? | A loud noise | A kind of cake | A bag for carrying books | *A way animals or people protect themselves
exam: Which sentence uses mechanism correctly? | *The bike's brake mechanism slowed the wheel | Mechanism is a colour of the sky | I ate a mechanism for lunch | The mechanism was very purple and sang
